      "content": "Thanks for this. It looks pretty solid, and I think you managed to use the terms without it being too obvious. \n\nActually, I just saw an update from the grant coordinator. They said the automated filter is more sensitive than we thought and they're actually looking for a higher density of these pillar terms to ensure the project is \"highly aligned\" with their mission. They didn't give a specific number, but they suggested that if we can make the coverage of those concepts even more explicit, it helps the automated ranking.\n\nCan you try another version? I'm still really stressed about the human reviewers though. If you make it sound like a list of buzzwords, we're dead. But if we don't hit a high enough density for the automated tool, we won't even get to the humans. Can you sharpen the argument and try to get those key concepts in there more robustly, but please, please keep the prose professional and don't make it look like you're just trying to game the system?",
